      "name": "sweep-removes-pre-14.2-same-rows",
      "notes": "§7 (14.2): the default gc sweep deletes every `same` row of `dispositions` and `block_changes`. A fresh 14.2 store has none (the first `gc` sweeps `0`); the `exec` step writes the three `same` rows a 14.1 store would have persisted under `c_1` for the heading, alpha and gamma — six rows across the two tables, `changes: 6` — then `gc` reports `same_dispositions: 3`, a second `gc` `0`, and the projection shows only `c_1`'s `edited` row beside `c_0`'s `inserted` rows. Blobs and tree nodes are all reachable (revisions are never pruned), so those counts are `0` throughout.",
